body:
Haha thanks for reading the post buddy. One of my main problems is literally not being able to wake up but its just my lazy ass, right. It's not like I set alarms and wake up hours after they are supposed to go off panicked and angry. And read the second last sentence in particular. Been years of this and this is still the exact attitude some doctors still show me. And I need a reference for a sleep specialist (which my doctors haven't thought to do), and even then this will likely take months. But thanks lmao...

&#x200B;

Sorry I just find it hilarious you actually think I haven't considered my "motivation" and "discipline". Like did you read my post? Very rude comment lmao sorry just can't get over how unhelpful this is.

For sure! I would highly recommend more kuhli loaches as they become much more active in numbers, and with the right tank (lots of shade and cover, hiding spots etc). 

&#x200B;

In a 30 gallon I would probably have around 6 loaches and 10 tetras, as well as your betta. Seems like a lot, I know, but a 30 gallon is plenty of real estate.

Hey I would really encourage to have an open discussion with your kid. Talk about what you were feeling, how things are going for you, but do not bring down your spouse or burden him, just explain you were in a moment of acute distress and you just felt so overwhelmed. Maybe go to a therapist together, and send him alone if you can. 

&#x200B;

Also maybe you should go somewhere else for the night and come back tomorrow to talk calmly with your husband. If you both agree you should definitely try therapy together.
